## ⬅️➡️ HTML → MaxUp Reverse Transpiler (`maxc --reverse`)

### Design principles
1. **Lossless round‑trip** — MaxUp → HTML → MaxUp must yield the original source (modulo whitespace normalisation).  
2. **Semantic recovery** — `<div class="card">` becomes `;.card`, `<h1>` becomes `#`, `<ul>`/`<li>` become `(`/`-`.  
3. **Heuristic, not brittle** — We parse HTML with a forgiving DOM (like `servo/html5ever`), then map node types to our token table.  

### New module: `reverse.rs`

```rust
// pseudocode architecture – ArchW1z style
use html5ever::parse_document;
use html5ever::rcdom::{RcDom, Handle, NodeData};

pub fn reverse_compile(html: &str) -> String {
    let dom = parse_document(RcDom::default(), Default::default())
        .from_utf8()
        .one(html.as_bytes());

    let mut max_source = String::new();
    walk_and_emit(&dom.document, 0, &mut max_source);
    max_source
}

fn walk_and_emit(handle: &Handle, indent: usize, out: &mut String) {
    let node = handle;
    match node.data {
        NodeData::Document => {
            for child in node.children.borrow().iter() {
                walk_and_emit(child, 0, out);
            }
        }
        NodeData::Element { ref name, ref attrs, .. } => {
            let tag = name.local.as_ref();
            let token = tag_to_max_token(tag);
            // write element token, then attributes as {attr="val"}, then children
            // if void element: trailing backslash
            // if text-only child: inline
            // else: newline+indent and colon fence (:::) for containers
        }
        NodeData::Text { ref contents } => {
            // escape and output literal text
        }
        // etc.
    }
}
